# The slider: a number the reader is choosing, on the scale of the numbers they could have
# chosen instead.
#
# A NUMBER setting used to be Left/Right over a preset list with the chosen value in the value
# column - "10m", and nothing at all about whether ten minutes was near the short end of what the
# field offers or near the long one. The figure still says how long; the track under it says how
# far along, and that is the half a column of durations cannot answer without the reader already
# carrying the list around.
#
# Watch Display first, where two rows carry one, and then LoRa - which is where the whole
# argument is on one screen: hop limit and transmit power get a track, and bandwidth, spreading
# factor and coding rate do not, because those numbers *name* a modem setting rather than
# measuring anything.

scene demo
scale 4
delay 200
config

tab settings
hold 500

# Display. Screen-on is ten minutes on a scale that runs from fifteen seconds to an hour; the
# carousel is off, which is the bottom of its own scale rather than off it - so it keeps its
# handle, hard left.
key down 4
hold 700
key a
hold 900

# Stepping it. The handle travels rather than jumping, because a press should be seen to land -
# and the value column and the track move together, since both are readings of one number.
key right
hold 700
key right
hold 700
key right 2
hold 900
key left 3
hold 1000

# The same control on every palette. The track is a role and the fill is a tone, so nothing here
# is switched by hand.
theme light
hold 900
theme contrast
hold 900
theme colorblind
hold 900
theme dark
hold 900

# And LoRa, where three of the five numbers deliberately have no track under them.
key b
hold 600
key down 3
hold 500
key a
hold 1200

# Transmit power reads "max", which is the firmware's word for "as much as this radio has". It is
# not the bottom of a power scale and it is not the top of one either, so the track draws its
# stops and puts no handle anywhere - and stepping off it brings one in from the low end, where
# 2 dBm actually is.
key down 8
hold 900
key right
hold 1200
